docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:63:> A BMI of 27 or above, particularly with a weight-related health condition, may be enough to start a conversation with our medical team about non-surgical options. Surgical options are usually discussed at higher BMI ranges; current MBS guidance for clinically severe obesity generally refers to BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with major co-morbidities, with suitability assessed by your surgeon.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:71:> Is weight loss surgery covered by Medicare in Australia? Medicare rebates may apply to eligible specialist consultations and some bariatric surgery items when current MBS criteria are met. Private health cover, waiting periods, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees still affect out-of-pocket costs, so our team gives you an itemised estimate before you make any decision.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:73:Why it matters: Medicare coverage needs a direct answer, not only a referral note.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:77:> The cost of weight loss surgery in Perth varies depending on the procedure, your level of private health cover, your hospital excess, and anaesthetist fees. Financing options such as Zip and TLC are also available for eligible patients.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:79:> The cost of weight loss treatment in Perth depends on the pathway: medical management, dietitian-led programs and surgery all have different fee structures, and surgical costs also vary by procedure, private health cover, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees. Some patients explore approved payment or funding pathways, but these should be discussed separately and should not influence whether treatment is clinically appropriate.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:101:> Options range from GLP-1 medications and structured very low calorie diets, to dietitian-led nutrition support, exercise guidance, endoscopic procedures, and surgery.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:119:> Whether that is a non-surgical weight loss program or a surgical alternative, we meet you exactly where you are.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:127:> From GLP-1 medications and structured diet programs through to sleeve, bypass, and band procedures, the weight loss treatment spectrum is broader than most people realise.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:129:> Weight loss treatment usually sits on a spectrum: medical management such as a supervised very low calorie diet, allied-health support such as dietitian care and exercise guidance, and surgical options such as gastric sleeve, gastric bypass or gastric band.
