     1	# Content Brief: Weight Loss Surgery Perth
     2	**URL:** /weight-loss-surgery-perth
     3	**Primary keyword:** weight loss surgery perth
     4	**Search intent:** informational / commercial
     5	**Target word count:** 1,100–1,400 words (matches brief; SERP is dominated by short-to-mid commercial clinic homepages, so the brief's depth is enough to compete while the spectrum-of-care breadth differentiates)
     6	
     7	## Page purpose
     8	This is the broadest, highest-traffic page on the site — it captures people who are at the very start of their research and are not yet attached to a specific procedure. Its job is to introduce the full spectrum of care (medical management through to surgery), make the reader feel seen and un-judged, and position OSWA as the team to help them work out what is right for them.
     9	
    10	## Keyword Intelligence
    11	
    12	### Primary Keyword
    13	- Keyword: weight loss surgery perth
    14	- AU Monthly Volume: 250
    15	- Keyword Difficulty: 45/100
    16	- CPC (AU): ~$1.3
    17	
    18	### Secondary Keywords (target naturally in body copy)
    19	| Keyword | AU Vol/mo | KD |
    20	|---|---|---|
    21	| bariatric surgery perth | 150 | 52 |
    22	| perth weight loss surgery | 100 | 46 |
    23	| weight loss surgery perth cost | 90 | 0 |
    24	| gastric bypass perth | 200 | 42 |
    25	| gastric band | 500 | 8 |
    26	| weight loss clinic perth | 100 | 2 |
    27	| weight loss doctor perth | 30 | 4 |
    28	| using super for weight loss surgery perth | 30 | 0 |
    29	
    30	### Semantic Terms to Include
    31	Comma-separated list of LSI/semantic terms the writer must naturally weave into the copy. These are not keyword-stuff targets — they are terms that signal topical depth to Google.
    32	
    33	bariatric surgery, gastric sleeve, sleeve gastrectomy, gastric bypass, adjustable gastric band, lap band, obesity as a medical condition, BMI, GLP-1 medication, very low calorie diet, dietitian support, type 2 diabetes, Medicare rebate, private health cover, endoscopic option, weight regain, Booragoon, Mandurah
    34	
    35	### SERP Landscape (AU)
    36	The SERP is almost entirely commercial: individual Perth bariatric surgeon and clinic homepages (Dr Siva Gounder / perthweightlosssurgery.com.au, perthbariatricsurgery.com.au / Dr Andrew Kiyingi, Advance Surgical / Jon Armstrong, Aurora Bariatrics / Dr Ruth Blackham, Dr Kevin Dolan, Perth Surgical & Bariatrics, Evolve Bariatrics). Domain ratings are low across the board (DR 1-26), so this is a winnable, weakly-defended SERP. Almost every result is a surgeon-led homepage selling a procedure menu — not informational guides. People Also Ask boxes surface clear informational intent: "How much does weight loss surgery cost in Perth?", "Is weight loss surgery covered by Medicare in Australia?", and "How much do I need to weigh to qualify for weight loss surgery?". Intent is mixed commercial + informational, which fits the brief's positioning of this as the broad top-of-funnel page.
    37	
    38	Top 5 ranking pages:
    39	| # | Domain | Page Title |
    40	|---|---|---|
    41	| 1 | perthweightlosssurgery.com.au | Perth Weight Loss Surgery — Dr Siva Gounder |
    42	| 2 | perthbariatricsurgery.com.au | Perth Bariatric Surgery — Dr Andrew Kiyingi |
    43	| 3 | advancesurgical.com.au | Weight Loss Surgery Perth — Advance Surgical (Jon Armstrong) |
    44	| 4 | aurorabariatrics.com.au | Aurora Bariatrics — Dr Ruth Blackham |
    45	| 5 | obesitysurgerywa.com.au | Weight Loss Surgery Perth — Obesity Surgery WA (OSWA, DR 11) |
    46	
    47	### Content Gap Opportunity
    48	Every top result is a surgeon homepage that funnels straight to surgery — none present medical management (GLP-1 medication, VLCD, dietitian support) as an equal pathway. That is OSWA's biggest differentiation opportunity and aligns exactly with the brief's mandate to frame obesity as a medical condition and not over-index on surgery. Second gap: the PAA boxes show high demand for cost, Medicare coverage, and BMI/eligibility answers, yet competitor homepages bury or omit these — directly addressing how medical management is assessed from BMI 27+, how Medicare rebates and MBS thresholds work, and how much treatment may cost / whether superannuation access can be explored in plain language (the brief already mandates an eligibility section, cost paragraph, and FAQs) will capture featured-snippet and PAA real estate competitors leave open. Third gap: low-DR competitors mean strong topical depth, empathetic non-judgemental framing, and a team-based (dedicated APD dietitian team, physicians + surgeons, 2 clinics) angle can outrank them without heavy backlinks. Note OSWA (obesitysurgerywa.com.au) currently sits at position 5 with DR 11, so this page is an existing-asset improvement play, not a cold start.
    49	
    50	### Recommended Word Count
    51	1,100-1,400 words (matches brief; SERP is dominated by short-to-mid commercial clinic homepages, so the brief's depth is enough to compete while the spectrum-of-care breadth differentiates).
    52	
    53	## Section guidance
    54	
    55	### Hero
    56	- Headline direction: Frame the page as covering more than just surgery — it is about finding the right starting point. The headline should signal expertise and approachability in the same breath.
    57	- Subheadline: 2–3 sentences. Acknowledge the emotional reality of years of trying (without framing the reader as a failure). Introduce OSWA as a team — surgeons, physicians, and dietitians — not just a surgical service. Make clear the team meets the reader where they are, including if they are not yet ready for surgery.
